# Commands this repository has that no document names, and why each is right
# to leave unwritten. Read by test_documented_commands.py, which fails on any
# other one. See DEVELOPERS.md#what-ci-proves.
#
# One paragraph per allowance: the comment saying why nobody should write it
# up, then the command on a line of its own, spelled as a document would spell
# it -- `manage.py <subcommand>` or `npm run <script>`. Naming it is what makes
# the omission a decision, and an entry that stops being needed is reported, so
# a command that has gone away or been documented after all cannot leave a
# stale line here.
#
# Keep it short. A long list is a set of documents that has stopped describing
# this repository, not a checker being fussy.

# Vite's own local preview of a production build. It takes no argument of ours
# and belongs to no path through this project: `npm run dev` is what a
# contributor runs and `npm run build` is what CI runs, so writing this up
# would be documenting Vite in somebody else's guide.
npm run preview

# Formatting without linting, for an editor to call on save. The command a
# person types is `npm run lint:fix`, which does both and is what
# DEVELOPERS.md prints; a second entry beside it in that table would be two
# answers to one question.
npm run format
